  "zinc_electroplated": "Light coating; not recommended for external use. Nuts must still meet 6H tolerance after coating.",
  "hot_dip_galvanised": "AS/NZS 1214 (modified adoption of ISO 10684): min average 50 um on threads. Bolts threaded to standard size; nuts tapped OVERSIZE after galvanising - clearance >= 4x coating thickness (effective diameter grows by 4x coating). Zinc-plated or plain nuts will not fit a galvanised bolt; galvanised nuts are too loose on plain/zinc bolts.",
  "hydrogen_embrittlement": "ISO 4042: HE investigation required where core/surface hardness > 320 HV (10.9, 12.9). Electroplated 10.9/12.9 must be baked within 4 h (typ. 200-230 C, 2-24 h); baking reduces but cannot eliminate risk. Recommendation: do not electroplate 10.9/12.9; use zinc flake or mechanical plating. GAA: electroplated bolts with Rm > 1000 MPa must be baked; mechanical plating and sherardising avoid HE."
