  "method": "Pull 'stretches' = As × min yield (bolt permanently stretches – the practical limit). Pull 'breaks' = As × min tensile (AS 4100 Ntf). Shear = 0.62 × min tensile × area (AS 4100 Cl. 9.3.2.1): 'thread' uses the root (minor-diameter) area when the threads sit in the joint line; 'shank' uses the full shank area when the plain shank sits in the joint line. Single shear plane. 1 kgf = 9.80665 N.",
  "warning": "These are ultimate BREAKING loads of a new bolt – not safe working loads. Structural design under AS 4100 uses φ = 0.8 on top; lifting needs rated hardware and much larger safety factors. Shock, bending, fatigue, corrosion and poor thread engagement all reduce real capacity.",
